{"id":"01a03ee1-540e-7dd3-8500-9dc2188ae76d","issue_id":"project-LICHEN-worker6-l1qw.11.3.1","event_type":"closed","actor":"Mark Atwood","old_value":"","new_value":"Superseded by the resolved single-primary address model: nodes self-derive exact 0200::/8 native /128 addresses, so RPL DODAG formation MUST NOT advertise 200::/7 (or 0200::/8) Prefix Information. Border-router global reachability is advertised with the RPL Grounded bit instead. Verified by Python gateway-reachability vectors (4 passed) and Rust gateway/root DIO tests (2 passed), which assert no Prefix Information option.","created_at":"2026-08-26T16:22:29.646907Z"}
